---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
import CommandBlock from '../../components/content/CommandBlock.astro';
import ScreenshotPlaceholder from '../../components/ui/ScreenshotPlaceholder.astro';
---

<GuideLayout 
  title="Gameplay Guide"
  guideType="gameplay"
>
  <h1>Gameplay Guide</h1>
  
  <h2>Opening the Menu</h2>
  <p>Press <strong>G</strong> (default) to open the MCDG menu from anywhere in-game. Or type <code>/mcdg</code> in chat (a clickable link is shown on join). All actions are available via the menu — no need to memorize commands.</p>
  <p>The keybind can be rebound in <strong>Options → Controls → MCDG</strong>.</p>

  <h2>Keybinds</h2>
  <p>All keybinds are rebindable in <strong>Options → Controls → MCDG</strong>.</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Key</th>
        <th>Action</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>G</td>
        <td>Open MCDG menu</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>M</td>
        <td>Add waypoint at current position (opens name/color screen)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>N</td>
        <td>Remove nearest waypoint</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>L</td>
        <td>Toggle waypoint labels</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>+/-</td>
        <td>Minimap size up/down</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <ScreenshotPlaceholder 
    title="MCDG Menu Interface"
    description="The MCDG menu showing all available actions"
    width="100%"
    height="300px"
  />

  <h2>Throwing Mechanics</h2>
  
  <h3>Throw Stances</h3>
  <p>MCDG supports three different throw stances, each with unique flight characteristics:</p>
  
  <h4>Overhand (Default)</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>No glide phase - direct ballistic trajectory</li>
    <li>Best for short, accurate throws</li>
    <li>Less affected by wind</li>
    <li>Good for approach shots and putting</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Backhand</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>Extended glide phase for maximum distance</li>
    <li>Standard throwing style for most players</li>
    <li>Best for long-distance drives</li>
    <li>More affected by wind during glide</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Forehand</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>Similar glide characteristics to backhand</li>
    <li>Alternative throwing style for different release angles</li>
    <li>Useful for specialized shot shapes</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Release Angles</h3>
  <p>Control the curve of your disc with three release angles:</p>
  
  <h4>Hyzer</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>Disc curves to the right (for right-handed backhand)</li>
    <li>Useful for controlled fade shots</li>
    <li>Good for fighting headwinds</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Flat</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>Neutral release with minimal curve</li>
    <li>Best for straight shots</li>
    <li>Most predictable flight path</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Anhyzer</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>Disc curves to the left (for right-handed backhand)</li>
    <li>Useful for tailwind shots</li>
    <li>Good for maximum distance with proper timing</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Power Charging</h2>
  <p>Hold right-click to charge your throw power:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Longer hold = more power (up to 100%)</li>
    <li>Power affects throw distance and disc speed</li>
    <li>Overcharge (125%) available with stamina system</li>
    <li>Audio cues indicate charge levels</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Reading the HUD</h2>
  
  <h3>Power Meter</h3>
  <p>Visual indicator showing current charge level when holding right-click.</p>

  <h3>Stance/Angle Display</h3>
  <p>Shows current throw stance and release angle for quick reference.</p>

  <h3>Minimap</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Shows hole layout, basket location, and your position</li>
    <li>Color-coded hazard overlays (water, sand, rough, etc.)</li>
    <li>Adjustable size with +/- keys</li>
    <li>Waypoint markers for custom navigation</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Scoring</h2>
  <p>MCDG uses traditional disc golf scoring:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Par</strong>: Expected number of throws for the hole</li>
    <li><strong>Birdie</strong>: One under par</li>
    <li><strong>Eagle</strong>: Two under par</li>
    <li><strong>Ace</strong>: Hole-in-one (one throw)</li>
    <li><strong>Bogey</strong>: One over par</li>
    <li><strong>Double Bogey</strong>: Two over par</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Rules / Surface Preset</h2>
  <p>Menu → <strong>Rules</strong> to view and change ruleset (Casual / Strict).</p>
  
  <h3>Strict Surface Presets</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Fast</strong> — Forgiving surface, less penalty for rough landings</li>
    <li><strong>Balanced</strong> — Default settings</li>
    <li><strong>Tournament</strong> — Hardest settings, strict landing enforcement</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Admin Tester Flow</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Join the world/server and press <strong>G</strong> to open the menu</li>
    <li><strong>Build a course:</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>Menu → <strong>Auto Build Course</strong> → type a name and press Enter</li>
        <li>(or: Menu → <strong>Manual Build Course</strong> for seed-based generation)</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Start a round:</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>Menu → Admin → <strong>Start Round</strong></li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Other players join:</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>Menu → <strong>Join Round</strong></li>
        <li>(or admin uses Menu → Admin → <strong>Join Round</strong> for all)</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>During play</strong>, if a player desyncs from the lie marker:
      <ul>
        <li>Menu → <strong>Go to Lie</strong> (or <code>/mcdg gotolie</code>)</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>View scores</strong> at any time:
      <ul>
        <li>Menu → <strong>Leaderboard</strong></li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>End and clean up</strong> after the test cycle:
      <ul>
        <li>Menu → <strong>End Round</strong> → Menu → Admin → <strong>Cleanup Course</strong></li>
      </ul>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Player Tester Flow</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Join the world/server and press <strong>G</strong> to open the menu</li>
    <li>Join an active round: Menu → <strong>Join Round</strong></li>
    <li>Play holes normally — throw your disc, walk to it, repeat</li>
    <li>Use Menu → <strong>Go to Lie</strong> if you need to teleport to your lie</li>
    <li>Save progress if leaving early: Menu → <strong>Save & Leave Round</strong></li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Advanced Commands</h2>
  <p>Some commands are intentionally hidden unless advanced mode is enabled.</p>
  
  <h3>Enable Advanced Commands</h3>
  <CommandBlock 
    command="MCDG_SHOW_ADVANCED_COMMANDS=true"
    description="Environment variable"
  />
  <CommandBlock 
    command="-Dmcdg.showAdvancedCommands=true"
    description="JVM property"
  />

  <h3>Typical Advanced Commands</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><code>resumecourse</code> — Resume a saved course session</li>
    <li><code>usecourse</code> — Select a specific course from catalog</li>
    <li><code>prunecourses</code> — Remove unused courses from catalog</li>
    <li><code>gotocourse</code> — Teleport to a specific course</li>
    <li><code>roundstatus</code> — Check current round status</li>
    <li><code>validateplacement</code> — Validate course placement</li>
    <li><code>buildcamp</code> — Build camp structure (deprecated)</li>
    <li><code>autotests</code> — Run automated placement tests</li>
  </ul>
</GuideLayout>
